<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yavne</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Yibna, Jamnia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yavne is a town on the coastal plain of Israel, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaffa">Jaffa</a>, known in antiquity as Jamnia. After the destruction of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temple-in-jerusalem">Second Temple</a> in 70 CE it became a centre of rabbinic learning. As Yibna, it was the site of the crusader castle of Ibelin, built by King Fulk in 1141, which gave its name to the powerful <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-ibelin">Ibelin family</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yavne.jpg" alt="Yavne" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Municipality of Yavne · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yavne_panoramic_view2.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
